Adjacent angles forming a right angle add to $90^{\circ}$.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\draw (0,0)--(40:2.2);
\draw (0.32,0)--(0.32,0.32)--(0,0.32);
\node at (1.17,0.43) {$a$};
\node at (0.53,1.13) {$b$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

A right angle is marked with a small **square**.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.9]
\usetikzlibrary{calc}
\draw (0,0)--(2.4,0);
\draw (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (X) at ($(O)!0.35cm!(2.4,0)$);
\coordinate (Y) at ($(O)!0.35cm!(0,2.4)$);
\draw (X)--($(X)+(Y)-(O)$)--(Y);
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
Find $x$. The two marked angles together form a right angle.

[tikz]\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\draw[black] (2.8,0)--(O)--(0,2.8);
\draw[black] (O)--(34:2.6);
\draw[black] (0.25,0)--(0.25,0.25)--(0,0.25);
\draw[black] (0:0.8) arc[start angle=0,end angle=34,radius=0.8];
\draw[black] (34:1.05) arc[start angle=34,end angle=90,radius=1.05];
\path (17:1.35) node {$34^{\circ}$};
\path (62:1.45) node {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}[/tikz]

Find $b$ in this rotated right angle. The square marks the angle between the outside arms.

